data_gese2
# Phase identity: layered beta-GeSe2 (GeSe2-I), standard P21/c:b1.
# Source structure: Materials Project mp-540625 experimental initial structure
# from matminer mp_all_20181018 snapshot (2018-10-18), CC BY 4.0.
# Artifact SHA-256: 1f3de2dc7c68959647240921b841293fce918ea1708e6f3760ba35a9cdfe0500
# https://materialsproject.org/materials/mp-540625/
# https://materialsproject.org/terms
# The snapshot axes were transformed losslessly as a'=A, b'=-C, c'=B and
# (x',y',z')=(x,-z mod 1,y), producing standard unique-b P21/c:b1. This is
# the initial experimental Dittmar-Schaefer structure, not the relaxed output
# and not tetragonal high-pressure COD 1521080.
# Primary structure: G. Dittmar and H. Schaefer, Acta Cryst. B32 (1976)
# 2726-2728, doi:10.1107/S0567740876008704.
# The catalog's B=0.6 A2 is an explicit placeholder, not an experimental value.
# Layered beta-GeSe2 cleaves on (001); the c-glide extinguishes odd 00l, so the
# catalog pins the first allowed parallel reflection (002).
# Validation: gese2-beta-p21c-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 21/c'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 14
_space_group_name_Hall '-P 2ybc'
_cell_length_a 7.016000
_cell_length_b 16.796000
_cell_length_c 11.8310003268
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.6500021204
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
